WEBVTT

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:10.110
Hear ye, all Gamindustri residents far and wide.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.930
We take one giant leap toward a new era today.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.290
It brings me great pleasure to be together with you all

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.080
as we welcome this joyous day.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.470
As you all know,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.930
this world has been torn by strife over the past few years.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.950
Lastation, governed by its CPU, the goddess Black Heart.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.110
Lowee, governed by its CPU, the goddess White Heart.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:56.030
Leanbox, governed by its CPU, the goddess Green Heart.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:06.040
And Planeptune, governed by myself, the goddess Purple Heart.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.710
Share Energy forms the basis of national power in this world.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.720
The four nations competed over it, and sometimes we goddesses ourselves came to blows.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.850
But now that will become
a thing of the past.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.670
The treaty of friendship that shall be signed today

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.990
will prohibit taking Share Energy by force.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:32.980
From this point onward, the only way to acquire it will be by making one's country a better place,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.490
which will lead to worldwide development and progress.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:45.870
We hereby swear to overcome the past and create a world filled with hope.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.300
Yahoo!

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.220
Done and dusted!

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.810
The difference between your two forms never fails to amaze me, Neptune.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.390
That aside, what'd you think of my speech, Noire?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.950
Well, it wasn't bad...

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.470
Though I'm pretty sure Histoire wrote it for you.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.290
It sure pisses me off that you got to hog the spotlight.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.290
C'mon, Blanc. Don't say that!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.270
I regret using rock-paper-scissors to decide the speaker.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.130
Why don't you just let it go?

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.760
Saying that now just makes you sound immature.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.650
She's right!

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.800
After all, we're no longer enemies!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.100
We're best buds now, right?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.850
A month has already passed since that amazing ceremony.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.050
You aren't fulfilling <i>any</i> of your
responsibilities as CPU, Neptune!

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.650
Sonic jump!

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.120
Fiddlesticks!

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.500
Well, I guess these peaceful days just turned my brain to mush!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.900
Neptune, CPUs have all kinds of work—

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.930
Sis!

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.750
Tea's ready!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.010
Thanks, Nepgear!

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.430
Wanna go head-to-head?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.010
Sure!

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.170
Not you too, Nepgear!

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.460
Knock it off!

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.510
Zoinks!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.970
Hey, the manual said not to do that!

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.020
Don't try this at home, kids!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.830
Iffy!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.120
Compa!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.170
Done with work?

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.330
Yes.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.210
I'm on my way to Nep-Nep's place.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.550
Oh, then I'll go with you.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.880
Under the right rules and regulations—

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.770
Take a look at this!

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.280
At the Share Crystal, not me!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.530
What about it?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.030
The amount of Share Energy gathered in our country's Share Crystal

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.540
is currently showing a downward trend.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.210
There's still a whole bunch.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.960
No need to worry, right?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.130
Of course there is!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.000
You know where we get Shares from, don't you?

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.050
Oh...

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.430
The feelings of trust that the citizens place in the CPU who rules them, right?

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.340
Indeed.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:15.350
This downward trend shows that our citizens are slowly falling out of love with Neptune!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.350
Say what?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.730
I don't remember doing anything that'd make them hate me.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.230
I don't think you've done anything recently that'd make them love you, either.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.320
W-Well...

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.650
Nepgear's right.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.240
We're sorry, Lady Histoire.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.910
We just happened to overhear the conversation.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.700
I don't mind if it's you two.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.200
Not you too, Iffy!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.960
Are you gonna take Histy's side as well?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.250
But you're different, right, Compa?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.000
Look at this, Nep-Nep.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:42.840
Huh?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.670
"We don't need goddesses."

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.420
Ack!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.880
In order to make these people understand you,

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.760
you need to work much harder at your job.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.060
She hit my weak point for massive damage!

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.260
I'm in big trouble!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.810
It's this <i>nation</i> that's in big trouble!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:03.190
For one thing, CPUs are supposed to devote all their blood, sweat, and tears to their citizens!

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:07.190
<i>That</i> is why you possess the great powers that you do.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:07.320
<i>Man, lectures are the worst.</i>

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.990
With great power comes great responsibility!

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.780
<i>How can I get away from here?</i>

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:14.780
<i>Oh, right!</i>

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.200
I'll go learn what it means to be a CPU!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:19.620
Huh?

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.420
Learn? From whom?

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.750
Uh... Noire!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:27.840
What?!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.590
Lastation's Noire!

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.680
I don't really get what's happening here, you see.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:42.190
Mind explaining to me why a neighboring country's CPU is sleeping at <i>our</i> Basilicom?!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.230
Oh, just pretend I'm not here and carry on with your job.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.360
I don't mind.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.530
Well, <i>I</i> do!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.950
We're so sorry, Noire.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.450
Sis!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.610
What's the big deal?

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.450
Aren't you here to learn what it means to be a CPU?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.450
Sorry, but I'll have to refuse.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.410
I don't intend to extend an olive branch to my enemies.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.290
Hey, I'm not your enemy!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.590
We signed a treaty of friendship!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.130
We're budd—

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.300
Doesn't change the fact that we're still competing over Share Energy.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.010
You're still my enemy.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.470
See, you keep saying all these totally uncute things!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.260
That's why people say you have no friends!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.560
I-I <i>do</i> have a friend!

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:20.890
Really?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:21.600
Who?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.890
Where are they from? What do they do?

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.190
Huh?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.270
Uh... Well...

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.780
I'm done with those documents, Sis.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.450
Hey there, Uni.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.200
Just put them over there.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.780
U-Um...

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.830
I was quite fast this time, wasn't I?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.370
I gave it my all—

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.580
Guess so.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.830
You've reached normal levels now, I suppose.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.040
Hey!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.540
Is Uni that so-called friend of yours?

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.960
I don't think you can call your sister a friend.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.090
You've got the wrong idea.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.970
I have other—

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.300
Really?

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.600
That's what you say, but aren't you just a loner?

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.390
No way!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.230
Nepgear...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.410
Sorry my sister had to butt in.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.320
Nah, it's fine.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.950
That's how Sis always is with me.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.830
Looks like she won't ever praise me unless I do a better job than she would.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.090
We all know that's just not gonna happen, though.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.170
Uni...

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.300
I can't even transform yet.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.220
That goes for me, Rom, and Ram too.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.390
I-I guess...

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.480
I'm sure I'll be the first out of the four of us to get the ability to transform.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.650
That's the spirit! I'm not gonna lose to you!

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.870
A text from Rom...

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.740
Why does she know I'm here in Lastation?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.750
I told her.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.750
She got really jealous.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:16.760
Nepgear and Uni must be having such a nice time hanging out together.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.010
Why can't <i>I</i> go visit another country?!

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.230
Don't be so selfish.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.770
I wanna go hang out with Nepgear and Uni too!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.530
I'm trying to work.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:37.280
Why?! Why?! Why?!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.240
Hey!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.620
Shut yer mouth!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.740
I said I was working! You friggin' deaf?!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.580
You're such a meanie.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.710
Let's go, Rom.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.590
Wait, Ram!

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.680
Sorry about that.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.600
Don't worry about it.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.560
We'd been fighting each other for a long time.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.110
But unlike us, your sisters are so innocent.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.570
I wonder if we can be friendlier to each other too.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.610
Just because we stopped using force

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.240
doesn't mean we can become the best of friends overnight.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.370
More importantly...

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:27.450
Yes, please allow me to continue with my proposal.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.040
Whoa!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.290
Stop!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.130
Get your hands off those documents!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.170
What?

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.260
But being a CPU starts with sorting out documents—

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.510
Do that at your <i>own</i> workplace!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.550
Tch.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:43.510
You're such a wet blanket.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.850
Where do you get off being so condescending?!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.060
Um...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:52.810
You've got monster hunting requests from your citizens, right?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:57.320
How about teaching Neptune what it means to be a CPU while we're at it?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:01.280
Oh, she wouldn't need to lay a finger on any of the documents that way.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.950
I suppose you're right.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.330
This looks good.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.830
It's nice and close to the border, too.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.290
Does that mean you're telling us to go back to Planeptune after we're done?

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.630
Well duh.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.210
I can't work with you around.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.510
All right, everyone!

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.420
Time to go monster hunting!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.550
Yeah!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.010
Wait, why are <i>you</i> acting like the leader?!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.220
We need to go monster hunting in two places.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.480
The Nursune Plains and the Trune Caves nearby.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.150
Both of them should be pretty easy to hand—

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:35.980
Sis.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:36.900
What?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.400
Nobody's listening.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.650
Gosh, I'm pooped!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.570
You okay, Compa?

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.280
Is this the famous "you can't read what it says from the back" sign?!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.910
Sis...

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.330
That's how most signs work.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.620
We're behind schedule.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.840
You take this way too seriously, Noire!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:12:59.420
Problem?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.260
Don't you ever get tired of it?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.430
It's no big deal.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.850
I want to create a much, <i>much</i> better nation.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.850
Well, so do I,

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.020
but I'd much rather have fun doing it.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.310
You have <i>too</i> much fun doing this!

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.440
She came!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.940
Ah, my goddess!

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.360
It's Black Heart!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.570
Oh no!

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.030
Access!

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:35.500
What?!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.250
You're gonna transform <i>now?!</i>

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.890
Rule number two of being a CPU:

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.520
let your people bear full witness to your majesty.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:58.020
Could you all give me some information about the monsters, please?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.770
You just transformed in front of them.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.650
What's so majestic about that?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.400
So this is the Nursune Plains, huh?

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.120
Yes. A mass outbreak of Dogoos here is causing a lot of problems.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.240
Understood.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.370
It seems Neptune and Nepgear, our neighbors from Planeptune,

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.710
will eliminate them for us.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:17.370
Zoinks!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.210
That came out of nowhere!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.290
We're supposed to do this?

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.090
Rule number 3:

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.260
show off at every opportunity.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.340
I'll take some pictures so you can use them as PR.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.390
This is such a pain.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.520
Though, well, these Dogoos are easy as pie to deal with.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.850
Let's do this!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.020
Nepgear!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.570
Okay, Sis!

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.180
Way to go, Nepgear!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:11.470
That's my sis!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.140
Thanks!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.270
Chest!

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.440
I'm gonna give it all I've got!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.910
There are way too many of them.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.540
We should help, Iffy!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:40.120
Right.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.290
Iffy! Compa!

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.880
Here I come!

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.220
Too good for them!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.810
We've basically won alread—

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.310
Sis,

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.980
we should help out—

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.020
Nope.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.070
The point is for them to deal with this themselves.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.910
Where do you think you're touching?!

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.990
Eww, majorly gross!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.040
Hey, stay out of there!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.420
This tickles!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.540
I'm gonna die!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.680
I...can't...

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.020
I'm gonna send your souls all the way back to Hell!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.030
Spectral Edge!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:54.950
Neptune...

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.700
Quit slacking.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.710
I don't even wanna look at jelly or meat buns for a while.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.170
Why didn't you activate your HDD form?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.840
Those Dogoos would have been easy pickings if you'd transformed!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.390
Well,

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.840
all's well that ends well, right?

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.930
You just had other people do your job for you!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.600
That's why your Share—

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:26.020
Fine, be as lazy as you want.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.110
I'll handle the rest myself.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.230
Show me the way to the Trune Caves.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.480
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.730
I'll go with you.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:34.860
No, that won't be necessary.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:37.240
Stay here and help these guys recover.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.280
'Kay.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.280
This way.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.580
Thanks.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.950
Noire's so short-tempered.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.200
Oh, Uni!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.000
Did you take any cool pics?

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.000
Wow!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.790
Super cute!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.050
They're going straight to my email address!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:53.880
Begone!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.350
A dead end, huh?

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.650
Guess I'm done here.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.030
An Ancient Dragon?!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.620
Quite the strong one, aren't we?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.870
Take this!

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.960
Hey there!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.420
You...

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:15.000
Why'd you go back to normal?

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.170
I'm not sure. It happened really suddenly—

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:17.800
Neptune!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.550
Noire.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.930
You're supposed to transform at times like <i>these</i>.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.230
Pay close attention!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.800
Behold the power of a goddess!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.840
Stop trying to act cool!

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:09.930
Thanks.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.940
Leave this one to me.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.530
Cross Combo!

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.100
I-I didn't need your help!

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.770
I would've been fine by myself.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.190
I'm sure.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.190
But helping each other is what friends do.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.480
It's not like I consider you a friend—

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.780
Why'd you choose this area?

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.150
Because I wanted you to leave—

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.280
Because you figured rumors would spread across the border

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.700
and Planeptune would hear about my valiant efforts?

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.240
That way, I could replenish some of my Share Energy.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.750
Thank you, Noire.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:25.470
But we also gotta let everyone know about the goddess who almost got her butt kicked!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.260
What?!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.180
Keep that a secret!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.970
Listen to this, guys!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:29.890
Hey!

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.220
Noire lost!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.310
We're friends, right?!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.520
Hey!

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.690
Black Heart and Purple Heart

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:43.190
killed the monsters with a hyper magic combo!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.700
Hooray!

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.740
That story gets crazier every time...

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.160
<i>Why did my transformation revert?</i>

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:58.460
Oh, so they purged all the monsters in the caves for us?

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.670
Now we can look for you-know-what without having eyes on the back of our heads.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:07.430
Amazing!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.150
I'd expect nothing less from Noire.

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.980
You mean "Neptune," right?

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:20.230
I'm still not convinced you're behind all this.

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:23.020
That's harsh, Histy!

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.280
What's wrong, Nepgear?

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:30.030
Someone put up some really weird pictures of me online.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:35.120
Huh? Those are all the pictures I sent to my email address!

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.040
You're so cute, Nepgear!

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:38.250
This is so embarrassing!

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:40.500
Are you sure you sent it to the right address?

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.420
Of course I did—

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.300
Oops.

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:45.510
I sent it to the address of a public mailing list...

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:46.720
I knew it.

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:49.720
But the response seems pretty positive!

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:52.350
"Visual shock"?

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.890
"It hit just the right spot"!

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:56.310
"Planeptune's still got a lot left in the tank."

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:58.100
Wow, people love it!

00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:58.770
Huh?

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:02.020
Don't tell me the reason our Share Energy went up so suddenly...

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:04.520
...was because of these pictures?!

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.230
You're amazing, Nepgear!

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:08.360
R-Really?

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:11.360
Then if we spread these things around even more...

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:11.910
Huh?

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.830
Do it for our Shares, Nepgear. For the Shares!

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:16.950
Hey, hold on, Sis!

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:20.500
I'm worried about where this country is headed in more ways than one.

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:22.380
I'll post it all over the place!

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:23.920
Stop!

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.590
Under the right rules and regulations—

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.930
Wh-What is this?

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:39.350
It's an explosion of art!
